            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "configurations/nvidia/vr_nvl72.json",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why are we using explicit addresses here instead of a $address variable in the Name field?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/nvidia/vr_nvl72.json",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Potin Lai",
                        "email": "potin.lai@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "potinlai"
                    },
                    "message": "Due to the linename of Leak GPIO pins (https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/88602/3), we are not able to use $address variable to replace \"B0\" & \"B1\".\n\n- HPM0\n - \"B0_vLeakDetect1Status0-I\"\n - \"B0_vLeakDetect1Status1-I\"\n\n- HPM1\n - \"B1_vLeakDetect1Status0-I\"\n - \"B1_vLeakDetect1Status1-I\"\n\n\nIt seems that a space is needed after the formula, otherwise the string will be incorrect.\n\nFor example: (address = 80)\n\"B$address - 80_vLeakDetect1Status0-I\"  --> \"B0\"\n\"B$address - 80 _vLeakDetect1Status0-I\"  --> \"B0 _vLeakDetect1Status0-I\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/nvidia/vr_nvl72.json",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "@ed@tanous.net or @spinler@us.ibm.com - Any ideas how to resolve this without duplicating the config for the two CPU boards?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/nvidia/vr_nvl72.json",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I can't think of anything, aside from adding support for {} or () around expressions or something along those lines."
                }
            ],
